## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE; apply it)
*Blocker:* a word added (a `title`, `aria-label` text, hint, caption, message, label or JSX text, or any readiness word); a figure, a draft body or a request that differs from main for the same inputs (H8); a path beyond the 5, or a HOLDS-path byte; a removed existing test line; a changed assertion in the one edited row; an existing test red at head and not at main, reproduced alone 3 times at head and 0 of 3 at main; a secret; a build or lint failure at head that is not at main; the head moved (a verdict is valid only at the head it ran on); a security-shaped finding is a STOP, never graded. *Major (class):* clause 1 or clause 2 of the acceptance NOT MET by your rows: a pricing-eligible caller can add a section while the read is pending (H1), a click after the answer starts without the default (H2, H3), the held state is never released after a success or after a failure (stranded button), a caller without the rights or a read answered without the grant is held (H4, H5), the two buttons are not held together (H6), or the hold ends on the shared `catalogueError` (GW10 not killed); a survivor of step 3's closed list (a row that does not turn red under the defect it names), except GW5 proved unreachable; a second racy existing test (step 4b); the edited row's wait hiding a regression that GW3 or GW8 does not turn red; a commit-message sentence FALSE against your measurement; a builder claim contradicted with a verdict consequence (the 15 new rows, 140 / 1368, "lost 0 added 15", "0 added literals", "29 of 30" if your measurement contradicts the rate). *Minor/Note:* **a pricing-eligible caller left with a disabled Add section and no explanation if the read never answers, with the existing pricing note saying "The server has not granted them to this sign-in." in that state (Minor: it is the ticket's own second branch and no new word was added on purpose; a finding for the product owner on whether words are needed, with the exact text and a fix-shape in prose that does not